York\nbe sold alongside with car seat alarm devices and a warning posting.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2020: S.8604 (Thomas) - Referred to Rules Committee/A.8582 (Paulin)\n\nReferred to Consumer Affairs and Protection Committee.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone noted to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome law.\n",
